Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Arq (.arq) file-association template - FP-012 reference material.
;
; This is NOT applied by any installer in this repository today (no
; Windows/Electron/Tauri shell exists yet - see docs/platform/DESKTOP-SHELL-PLAN.md
; and docs/platform/FILE-ASSOCIATION-PLAN.md). A real Windows packaging step must:
;   1. Replace the two "C:\Program Files\Arq\Arq.exe" paths below with the real
;      installed executable path (or generate this fragment from the installer's
;      own install directory at install time).
;   2. Merge/import this fragment as part of installation, not ship it standalone.
;
; Extension: .arq
; MIME type: application/vnd.arq.project+sqlite
; ProgID:    Arq.Project.1
;
; This registry entry only controls what the OS launches on double-click. Arq
; itself must still independently verify the real SQLite application_id
; (0x41525131, "ARQ1") before trusting the file's contents - see
; packages/file-ingress/src/native-arq-header.ts's inspectNativeArqHeader.
; A file merely named *.arq is never trusted on the strength of this
; association alone.
;
; Per-user (HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes) rather than machine-wide
; (HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT) so this fragment can be applied without administrator
; rights, per current Windows guidance for app file-type registration. A full
; production installer additionally registers under
; HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\RegisteredApplications and a per-app Capabilities
; key so Arq appears in Windows' "Default apps" picker - omitted here as
; that dance depends on the real installer's own app registration name, which
; does not exist yet.

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\.arq]
@="Arq.Project.1"
"Content Type"="application/vnd.arq.project+sqlite"

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\Arq.Project.1]
@="Arq Project"

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\Arq.Project.1\DefaultIcon]
@="\"C:\\Program Files\\Arq\\Arq.exe\",0"

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\Arq.Project.1\shell\open\command]
@="\"C:\\Program Files\\Arq\\Arq.exe\" \"%1\""
